00:51:03.184 --> 00:51:08.846
And I strongly encourage history chapter one of his Theory of the Universal Wave Function,

00:51:08.846 --> 00:51:11.685
available in The Many Worlds Interpretation by DeWitt and Graham.

00:51:11.685 --> 00:51:19.406
He says that there's these two rules, let's look at what happens if we only apply rule

00:51:19.406 --> 00:51:26.034
number one. Very nice question. And he was probably not the first to ask this question.

00:51:26.034 --> 00:51:27.947
There's evidence that Schrödinger thought about that.

00:51:27.947 --> 00:51:30.080
Yes, applying his equation all the way through.

00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:34.400
There's actually a quote where he says that he thought it was,

00:51:34.400 --> 00:51:40.739
I think, apparently ridiculous to apply rule one at certain points and rule two at other points.

00:51:40.739 --> 00:51:48.112
Everett was probably the first one who realized that applying rule one all the way through

00:51:48.112 --> 00:51:49.360
is not contradictory.

00:51:49.360 --> 00:51:51.440
Yeah, it's elegant and self-consistent.

00:51:51.440 --> 00:51:55.671
So let's do it, just quickly, so we kind of go through this solution to the measurement

00:51:55.671 --> 00:51:57.867
problem by Everett.

00:51:57.867 --> 00:52:00.370
So how did he apply just rule one, right?

00:52:00.370 --> 00:52:04.665
He said, okay, we have a quantum system we care to measure, say a spin.

00:52:04.665 --> 00:52:07.280
That's a typical system, especially back in the '50s.

00:52:07.280 --> 00:52:11.960
A silver atom has some spin. You can prepare it spinning one way,

00:52:11.960 --> 00:52:15.944
spinning another way, and when you throw it in a magnetic field,

00:52:15.944 --> 00:52:20.523
if it's spinning, say, clockwise, it's going to go up, and if it's spinning counterclockwise,

00:52:20.523 --> 00:52:24.889
it's going to go down, in the inhomogeneous magnetic field.

00:52:24.889 --> 00:52:30.221
This setup is known as a Stern-Gerlach measurement apparatus.

00:52:30.221 --> 00:52:36.624
And what happens: if you spin it clockwise, it goes up, and then you have a detector

00:52:36.624 --> 00:52:42.835
that is going to be hit by the trajectory of the atom going upwards.

00:52:42.835 --> 00:52:48.090
The detector is made of atoms. So we're going to have to apply quantum theory to the

00:52:48.090 --> 00:52:50.000
first atom of the detector.

00:52:50.000 --> 00:52:52.673
Yes.

00:52:52.673 --> 00:52:57.053
So Everett also had this nice idea that you don't need to resolve the partial differential

00:52:57.053 --> 00:53:00.365
equations to have an exact solution to tell what's going to happen.

00:53:00.365 --> 00:53:06.528
You can kind of use bras and kets in a coarse-grained way, which is getting you the right

00:53:06.528 --> 00:53:08.582
story without solving the precise microphysics.

00:53:08.582 --> 00:53:13.698
So the idea is that, well, if the atom is going upwards, just before it hits the detector,

00:53:13.698 --> 00:53:17.173
the first atom of the detector is unexcited, but a second after,

00:53:17.173 --> 00:53:22.372
or a fraction of a second after, the first atom is going to be excited.

00:53:22.372 --> 00:53:29.788
And meanwhile, note that the atoms that are building the detector on the downward path

00:53:29.788 --> 00:53:34.365
are unexcited. So if you are to characterize everything quantum mechanically,

00:53:34.365 --> 00:53:40.075
not just the silver atom, but also the atoms in the detector that is up there,

00:53:40.075 --> 00:53:46.009
the detector that is down there, well, you have this nice state where the atom was spinning

00:53:46.009 --> 00:53:50.906
clockwise, it went upwards, and it has excited the first atom of the upward detector,

00:53:50.906 --> 00:53:52.834
left the downward detector unchanged.

00:53:52.834 --> 00:53:58.091
And then you keep advancing time, and there's a cascade reaction in the atoms of the

00:53:58.091 --> 00:54:02.340
upward detector, to the point that it couples to green light.

00:54:02.340 --> 00:54:07.900
And then this green light eventually reaches your retina, but light and retinas and optic

00:54:07.900 --> 00:54:10.100
nerves are also quantum mechanical systems.

00:54:10.100 --> 00:54:13.854
So Everett said, "Now I'm not reaching the observer, I'm still...

00:54:13.854 --> 00:54:18.920
Guess what? I'm still going to use quantum mechanics to study what happens to the observer.

00:54:18.920 --> 00:54:23.980
I'm not going to retreat into, 'And then some magic unicorn happens.'" No,

00:54:23.980 --> 00:54:27.140
no, no. Let's bite the bullet, carry through.

00:54:27.140 --> 00:54:30.980
And you read, well, if the atom spins counterclockwise, well,

00:54:30.980 --> 00:54:35.774
then, the big chain reaction, eventually the wave function, or the way we're describing

00:54:35.774 --> 00:54:39.260
quantum mechanically the collection of atoms that is composing an observer,

00:54:39.260 --> 00:54:43.140
is going to be in a state that has seen green light.

00:54:43.140 --> 00:54:47.220
It gets entangled with that state. And so progressively you get a chain of entanglements

00:54:47.220 --> 00:54:52.780
that grows until it progressively becomes a separate branch.

00:54:52.780 --> 00:54:56.429
You're slightly ahead of my story. Because right now I said,

00:54:56.429 --> 00:55:01.300
what if the atom spins clockwise? I'm only studying the clockwise case.

00:55:01.300 --> 00:55:04.747
And if you only study the clockwise case, technically there's no entanglement,

00:55:04.747 --> 00:55:08.920
because everything can factor out. And then we could do the counterclockwise case,

00:55:08.920 --> 00:55:11.460
and then we study what happens. And while the atom will go downwards,

00:55:11.460 --> 00:55:15.040
it will hit the downward detector, but not the upward detector,

00:55:15.040 --> 00:55:19.100
and it will be coupled to a red light. And you and I will see red light,

00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:24.500
and we'll be in a state where our body, especially our degrees of freedom in our brains,

00:55:24.500 --> 00:55:27.860
are compatible with the fact that we've recorded red light.

00:55:27.860 --> 00:55:28.420
Right.

00:55:28.420 --> 00:55:32.340
And entanglement comes in when you say, "Oh, well, quantum mechanical systems can be

00:55:32.340 --> 00:55:34.792
not only spinning clockwise or counterclockwise.

00:55:34.792 --> 00:55:39.620
They can be in a state that they're spinning clockwise plus spinning counterclockwise."

00:55:39.620 --> 00:55:42.380
Yes, this is just a superposition of quantum systems.

00:55:42.380 --> 00:55:49.493
And it's obviously an irreducible element of the theory that's required to explain much

00:55:49.493 --> 00:55:51.676
of the phenomena we have in quantum theory.

00:55:51.676 --> 00:55:56.100
So we prepare this atom spinning clockwise plus spinning counterclockwise and see what happens.

00:55:56.100 --> 00:56:02.475
And you were right to bring up linearity earlier, because by linearity of the Schrödinger

00:56:02.475 --> 00:56:07.553
equation, what we have is that if you have a solution to what happens when it spins clockwise...

00:56:07.553 --> 00:56:08.053
Right.

00:56:08.053 --> 00:56:11.666
And you have a solution to what happens when it spins counterclockwise,

00:56:11.666 --> 00:56:16.580
well, when you're adding those two initial conditions, the atom is spinning clockwise

00:56:16.580 --> 00:56:21.615
plus it's spinning counterclockwise, then the solution to the Schrödinger equation is

00:56:21.615 --> 00:56:25.700
just that you have to carry on each of these trajectories in your terms.

00:56:25.700 --> 00:56:26.900
Yeah, separately.

00:56:26.900 --> 00:56:30.320
So this is where you start getting into a huge entangled state,

00:56:30.320 --> 00:56:35.300
because, as I said, Everett was in the business of applying physics to the whole thing,

00:56:35.300 --> 00:56:37.852
not just to the little thing we call the silver atom.

00:56:37.852 --> 00:56:41.202
And so the quantum state of the whole thing evolves into, roughly speaking,

00:56:41.202 --> 00:56:45.620
because I'm going to use the past verb tense to make the story simpler,

00:56:45.620 --> 00:56:51.753
but it evolves into: the atom was spinning clockwise, it went upwards,

00:56:51.753 --> 00:56:56.825
it hit the upward detector atoms but not the downward detector atoms,

00:56:56.825 --> 00:57:03.140
it emitted green light but not red light, and Charles saw green light and he didn't see

00:57:03.140 --> 00:57:04.020
red light...

00:57:04.020 --> 00:57:04.520
Yes.

00:57:04.520 --> 00:57:09.900
Plus the other case: it went downwards, it hit the down detector,

00:57:09.900 --> 00:57:13.195
not the up detector, it emitted red light, not green light, and Charles saw red light,

00:57:13.195 --> 00:57:14.079
not green light.

00:57:14.079 --> 00:57:14.579
Yes.

00:57:14.579 --> 00:57:19.424
And this is an entangled state, because these two terms cannot be factored,

00:57:19.424 --> 00:57:24.252
one for each system. And if we look at the progression of these two terms,

00:57:24.252 --> 00:57:29.281
we have a branching structure. For example, initially, before my retina saw light,

00:57:29.281 --> 00:57:33.828
I was still a Charles in an "I haven't seen any light" state,

00:57:33.828 --> 00:57:39.512
and as soon as the two terms are propagating in time, well, then I branch into a Charles

00:57:39.512 --> 00:57:43.826
sees green light and a Charles sees red light, in a different term of the wave function.

00:57:43.826 --> 00:57:47.877
Right. So now we have two Charleses, one that saw the green light,

00:57:47.877 --> 00:57:53.705
one that saw the red light, and eventually that entire element is going to keep growing,

00:57:53.705 --> 00:57:56.514
of course, until it takes up the whole universe.

00:57:56.514 --> 00:57:59.620
Yeah, because not only Charles is the witness of this measurement.

00:57:59.620 --> 00:58:02.786
And I think that's a very important lesson, is that we're not putting the observer at

00:58:02.786 --> 00:58:03.940
the center of anything here.

00:58:03.940 --> 00:58:06.180
Right, we're just one other recording device.

00:58:06.180 --> 00:58:12.809
Yes. But as many of the luminaries of this studying the emergence of the classicality

00:58:12.809 --> 00:58:17.371
program have pointed out, all of these witnesses, like the photon fields,

00:58:17.371 --> 00:58:21.740
is going to be also carrying information about the green light that was emitted.

00:58:21.740 --> 00:58:27.417
And therefore, what turns out happening is that these two terms of the wave function,

00:58:27.417 --> 00:58:33.551
for all practical purposes, have no chance to re-interact together.

00:58:33.551 --> 00:58:37.574
Because to have two terms of the wave function re-interact together,

00:58:37.574 --> 00:58:41.209
you need to find a way to put them back into a common state.

00:58:41.209 --> 00:58:41.709
Yes.

00:58:41.709 --> 00:58:45.180
But now there's so many witnesses that have witnessed the outcome is up,

00:58:45.180 --> 00:58:48.260
and one of the new developments we can deduct them down.

00:58:48.260 --> 00:58:53.131
There's no chance of re-interfering that into a quantum experiment to produce a sharp outcome.

00:58:53.131 --> 00:58:56.547
Unlike what would happen for a person inside a quantum computer,

00:58:56.547 --> 00:59:00.025
who would be perfectly shielded from this environmental interaction.

00:59:00.025 --> 00:59:05.149
It will evolve into a collection of persons, or states, for the quantum computer,

00:59:05.149 --> 00:59:08.707
and the idea of a quantum computer is to keep those coherent,

00:59:08.707 --> 00:59:12.848
shielded from the environment, so that they can re-interfere back and produce a common state.

00:59:12.848 --> 00:59:13.348
Yes.

00:59:13.348 --> 00:59:16.955
It is only explainable with the various terms of the wave function,

00:59:16.955 --> 00:59:20.220
the various worlds. Now here are these two worlds.

00:59:20.220 --> 00:59:26.200
They're separated, and so for all practical purposes, forget the other ones.

00:59:26.200 --> 00:59:31.994
Yeah, because the entanglement, as it grows, starts growing more exponentially,

00:59:31.994 --> 00:59:34.696
because more and more particles get entangled with it.

00:59:34.696 --> 00:59:38.651
And so if you were to try to come back to the initial state,

00:59:38.651 --> 00:59:43.220
it gets harder and harder, because you have to put them back in the original states,

00:59:43.220 --> 00:59:48.040
which becomes exponentially harder as you get more and more particles,

00:59:48.040 --> 00:59:50.954
and it takes a lot of the particles, and it just gets worse and worse.

00:59:50.954 --> 00:59:57.000
But putting it all back to the initial state is one way of creating interference.

00:59:57.000 --> 00:59:58.384
Yes.

00:59:58.384 --> 01:00:02.738
But another valid way of calling it interference is to put it into the same state.

01:00:02.738 --> 01:00:03.238
Yes.

01:00:03.238 --> 01:00:05.604
But since they're so different on so many degrees of freedom,

01:00:05.604 --> 01:00:08.313
it's for all practical purposes impossible to do so.

01:00:08.313 --> 01:00:14.134
And I believe this is the point where even today prominent physicists are still confused,

01:00:14.134 --> 01:00:19.277
is that they still take Schrödinger's reductio ad absurdum argument seriously.

01:00:19.277 --> 01:00:24.163
So suppose, I'm no historian, I haven't studied these letters,

01:00:24.163 --> 01:00:29.157
but suppose Schrödinger went as far as to consider the fact that if he applies his equation

01:00:29.157 --> 01:00:35.960
all the way through, you would get to an observer in a superposition of states.

01:00:35.960 --> 01:00:42.916
I think the very legit idea here is to say, "Oh, but that's nonsense."

01:00:42.916 --> 01:00:44.402
Yeah.

01:00:44.402 --> 01:00:47.986
Because we only observe one outcome, right?

01:00:47.986 --> 01:00:53.073
We never observe some form of superposition of cat is dead and alive simultaneously.

01:00:53.073 --> 01:00:56.593
So we never observe red and green light simultaneously, in my example.

01:00:56.593 --> 01:00:59.696
So that's nonsense, and therefore Everett's program cannot hold.

01:00:59.696 --> 01:01:00.196
Yes.

01:01:00.196 --> 01:01:03.765
But then I think you know the answer. What did Everett say?

01:01:03.765 --> 01:01:07.320
I don't know what specifically Everett said here, but it's not because you don't see

01:01:07.320 --> 01:01:11.568
the other outcome that it's not true. Well, the mathematical terms are there,

01:01:11.568 --> 01:01:13.400
so you need to take them literally.

01:01:13.400 --> 01:01:16.340
Yeah, that's an important piece of the explanation.

01:01:16.340 --> 01:01:19.300
And I think another one is also: study your whole structure.

01:01:19.300 --> 01:01:23.800
I have these two states with many witnesses of the green light,

01:01:23.800 --> 01:01:28.400
"I saw green light," da-da-da-da-da, plus many witnesses of the red light,

01:01:28.400 --> 01:01:36.600
"I saw red light." Nowhere in this structure there is a Charles who sees both lights.

01:01:36.600 --> 01:01:41.028
There's only a Charles who sees green light, and elsewhere there's a Charles who sees

01:01:41.028 --> 01:01:45.618
red light. But nowhere we have this thing we were worried about,

01:01:45.618 --> 01:01:48.703
which was that we're going to observe a superposition.

01:01:48.703 --> 01:01:49.853
No, we don't.

01:01:49.853 --> 01:01:50.353
Yeah.

01:01:50.353 --> 01:01:56.944
We only observe one outcome. And plus, we can cash out many of the features of the collapse.

01:01:56.944 --> 01:02:01.336
For example, if we re-measure our quantum system, well, the Charles who has measured

01:02:01.336 --> 01:02:05.840
green light... So for example, I still have access to my silver atom and I re-measure it.

01:02:05.840 --> 01:02:10.612
Well, then, because I'm in that term, I'm going to re-measure that the atom was spinning clockwise.

01:02:10.612 --> 01:02:11.112
Yes.

01:02:11.112 --> 01:02:13.529
And so we have the illusion of a collapse.

01:02:13.529 --> 01:02:14.988
You're entangled.

01:02:14.988 --> 01:02:16.375
Yeah, well, we have a collapse.

01:02:16.375 --> 01:02:16.875
Yes.

01:02:16.875 --> 01:02:20.304
And in the other branch of the wave function, well, then I'm going to re-measure that

01:02:20.304 --> 01:02:21.168
it's spinning counterclockwise.

01:02:21.168 --> 01:02:21.744
Yes.

01:02:21.744 --> 01:02:24.960
And that's why we also have intersubjective agreement in the multiple observers.

01:02:24.960 --> 01:02:28.635
Because if you were also sitting next to me, if I see green light,

01:02:28.635 --> 01:02:30.706
you'll also see green light, because we got entangled together.

01:02:30.706 --> 01:02:34.772
But that's written in your theory. So it's a very important objection,

01:02:34.772 --> 01:02:40.711
"But we don't see two outcomes, so this is ridiculous." But then the beauty is that we

01:02:40.711 --> 01:02:45.162
used the same theory, namely quantum mechanics in the fully unitary regime,

01:02:45.162 --> 01:02:46.306
to answer that.

01:02:46.306 --> 01:02:51.663
It's a beautiful story. But in the early days of these debates on Everett,

01:02:51.663 --> 01:02:57.928
I don't want to dare to claim who it was, but at some point somebody said,

01:02:57.928 --> 01:03:02.619
"But this precise thing, we don't feel branching, we don't feel multiple outcomes." And

01:03:02.619 --> 01:03:10.922
the argument that was made was, well, Newton's theory, enlightened also with heliocentrism,

01:03:10.922 --> 01:03:17.440
says that the Earth is a spinning ball, and we have a valid concern:

01:03:17.440 --> 01:03:21.451
hold on, if it was a spinning ball, we would feel it, right?

01:03:21.451 --> 01:03:23.303
We would feel the ball spinning.

01:03:23.303 --> 01:03:23.920
Yeah.

01:03:23.920 --> 01:03:29.543
Very valid point. And the answer is not to declare, "You will not feel it." It is to calculate.

01:03:29.543 --> 01:03:32.762
Hold on, let me take your objection seriously.

01:03:32.762 --> 01:03:40.120
You calculate, and according to Newton's laws and the velocity of one turn per day of

01:03:40.120 --> 01:03:44.632
the Earth and the radius of the Earth, you realize that, well,

01:03:44.632 --> 01:03:47.333
for your own little life, you would not feel it.

01:03:47.333 --> 01:03:47.833
Yes.

01:03:47.833 --> 01:03:51.813
But by the way, thanks for pointing it out, because we have Coriolis forces and so on.

01:03:51.813 --> 01:03:55.547
And in fact, it's a very valid point, and we learn stuff from this.

01:03:55.547 --> 01:03:56.047
Yes.

01:03:56.047 --> 01:03:59.091
But it's not an uppercut. In fact, it survives this test.

01:03:59.091 --> 01:03:59.591
Yes.

01:03:59.591 --> 01:04:03.586
And many things here happen too in quantum theory, where we don't feel branching.

01:04:03.586 --> 01:04:09.883
But then the most interesting parts of these emergence of quasi-classical regimes are

01:04:09.883 --> 01:04:14.931
when they're in fact quasi-classical, namely, we don't send orthogonal states to orthogonal

01:04:14.931 --> 01:04:20.139
states, but we let a little bit of fuzzy quantumness in the way the two terms slowly

01:04:20.139 --> 01:04:23.903
separate, and we observe weak quantum effects.

01:04:23.903 --> 01:04:28.008
And it gives rise to a classical reality, which is even more compelling,

01:04:28.008 --> 01:04:33.568
because it's basically exactly like our own, because it gives rise to some emergent classical structures.

01:04:33.568 --> 01:04:39.470
But if you would look at places in your emergent structures where they're sort of shielded

01:04:39.470 --> 01:04:44.295
from this vastly entangling, many witnesses of the measurement outcomes,

01:04:44.295 --> 01:04:47.074
you would see some form of quantum effects.

01:04:47.074 --> 01:04:50.091
And guess what, this is the world we live in.

01:04:50.091 --> 01:04:54.736
If you start looking at very small structures, we have weak quantum effects.

01:04:54.736 --> 01:04:59.195
But it's not because... and that's another misconception of quantum theory.

01:04:59.195 --> 01:05:02.113
It's not because quantum theory only applies to the small.

01:05:02.113 --> 01:05:06.754
It applies to everything. It's just that these characteristically quantum effects of

01:05:06.754 --> 01:05:11.472
interference are not going to be observed once massive witnesses have entangled.

01:05:11.472 --> 01:05:15.360
Yes, but they're still observable at a small scale.

01:05:15.360 --> 01:05:22.800
Tie back to our original Bell, Bob and Alice, what is the explanation then for how they're

01:05:22.800 --> 01:05:26.142
able to get to the 85 percent?

01:05:26.142 --> 01:05:33.002
In quantum theory, as we said earlier, these entangled systems are defined such that

01:05:33.002 --> 01:05:39.280
they have one common wave function for two particles, and these two particles could actually

01:05:39.280 --> 01:05:44.763
be remote. And so if you look at what's the branching structure that gives rise to that:

01:05:44.763 --> 01:05:50.594
if Alice and Bob are sharing an entangled state, say 00 plus 11,

01:05:50.594 --> 01:05:56.711
what happens is that when Alice would measure, this whole state would evolve into:

01:05:56.711 --> 01:06:04.230
Alice's system is zero, Bob's system is zero, and Alice measured that her system is zero,

01:06:04.230 --> 01:06:10.252
plus Alice's system is one, Bob's system is one, and Alice measured that her system is one.

01:06:10.252 --> 01:06:14.740
And then we have these two sort of worlds generating.

01:06:14.740 --> 01:06:16.800
So they get entangled with the measurements.

01:06:16.800 --> 01:06:22.320
She gets entangled with the measurement, but she also gets entangled with Bob's particle.

01:06:22.320 --> 01:06:23.440
Right, yeah.

01:06:23.440 --> 01:06:28.560
And so if you jump in Alice's shoes, and you're like, "I'm Alice who saw one,

01:06:28.560 --> 01:06:29.200
outcome one."

01:06:29.200 --> 01:06:30.200
Yes.

01:06:30.200 --> 01:06:35.922
"And for a strange reason, I'm in the same branch as Bob's particle,

01:06:35.922 --> 01:06:38.440
which will be in state one."

01:06:38.440 --> 01:06:40.440
Yes, yes. Okay.

01:06:40.440 --> 01:06:46.215
And so this is where the nature of entanglement in the Schrödinger picture portrays a

01:06:46.215 --> 01:06:51.640
somewhat misleading account of these branching effects, that may in fact look non-local.

01:06:51.640 --> 01:06:57.070
Again, it's not a non-locality of literally having an action there,

01:06:57.070 --> 01:07:03.820
but it's strange that Alice, who sees one, right away is in the world with Bob's particle

01:07:03.820 --> 01:07:10.220
being one. And suppose that Bob would also be measuring, Bob one would also be in the story.

01:07:10.220 --> 01:07:15.120
And so Alice one and Bob one would be right away identified across space.

01:07:15.120 --> 01:07:17.380
There we go. Crash course on Heisenberg quantum mechanics.

01:07:17.380 --> 01:07:22.880
So quantum theory was discovered twice, first by Heisenberg and then by Schrödinger.

01:07:22.880 --> 01:07:27.699
Heisenberg's story was a story of: we're going to have our physical quantities we care

01:07:27.699 --> 01:07:31.420
about, and we're going to promote them to matrices.

01:07:31.420 --> 01:07:36.520
So things like spin of something, which was just a discrete structure in a classical

01:07:36.520 --> 01:07:44.136
theory, now is a matrix. Things like position is also going to be encoded as a very,

01:07:44.136 --> 01:07:47.720
very large matrix, infinite-dimensional operator-valued.

01:07:47.720 --> 01:07:50.140
I don't want to dive into the math, there's no point for it.

01:07:50.140 --> 01:07:56.280
But in short, it's a story of: we describe physical objects as time-evolving matrices.

01:07:56.280 --> 01:08:01.285
And Schrödinger came up with his wave mechanics account, which was very different.

01:08:01.285 --> 01:08:06.389
Things are waves, or wave functions, and they evolve in time according to such and such properties.

01:08:06.389 --> 01:08:12.836
Now, the work of John von Neumann was huge, because he managed to build the mathematical

01:08:12.836 --> 01:08:21.310
arena, okay, he was not alone, but to build a mathematical arena that could kind of unify

01:08:21.310 --> 01:08:26.138
those two theories together, with these so-called structures of Hilbert spaces,

01:08:26.138 --> 01:08:30.520
and bounded operators, and vectors in Hilbert spaces.

01:08:30.520 --> 01:08:35.791
And the short story is that a calculation in quantum mechanics looks like that,

01:08:35.791 --> 01:08:42.172
where you have a state vector here. For the viewer, this would be a ket.

01:08:42.172 --> 01:08:48.289
This would be a bra. It's confusing. So these are the wave function thing.

01:08:48.289 --> 01:08:53.569
And in the middle, there's a bunch of matrices, and then you have also evolution operators

01:08:53.569 --> 01:08:57.960
in the middle. So you have a state vector, evolution operator,

01:08:57.960 --> 01:09:00.360
matrix, evolution operator, state vector.

01:09:00.360 --> 01:09:05.560
And then the Schrödinger view says, "Oh, the evolution operators,

01:09:05.560 --> 01:09:08.493
the unitary evolutions, they should apply to the state vectors,

01:09:08.493 --> 01:09:11.901
to these wave functions." And the Heisenberg picture view is to say,

01:09:11.901 --> 01:09:15.580
"Oh no, we should evolve the matrices in the middle." And typically,

01:09:15.580 --> 01:09:21.044
because all calculations in quantum theory have this form, we realize that it doesn't

01:09:21.044 --> 01:09:25.971
really matter. If what you're after is to compute a number, you can have it the way you run.

01:09:25.971 --> 01:09:28.714
You can have the unitary operators acting this way or that way,

01:09:28.714 --> 01:09:31.489
but you're going to get the same number, because this calculation here,

01:09:31.489 --> 01:09:35.180
this sandwich I'm making up with my hands, at the end of the day,

01:09:35.180 --> 01:09:38.540
it's a number. And so von Neumann declared the two theories to be equivalent.

01:09:38.540 --> 01:09:45.504
But as I like to point out in my latest chapter in the book by Alyssa Ney,

01:09:45.504 --> 01:09:50.943
edited by... the book is titled Local Quantum Mechanics, Oxford University Press,

01:09:50.943 --> 01:09:52.840
just released last month.

01:09:52.840 --> 01:09:53.560
Buy it.

01:09:53.560 --> 01:09:59.610
It's a good book, yeah. That argument that von Neumann made,

01:09:59.610 --> 01:10:05.720
and that the physics community took for granted, is an instrumentalist argument.

01:10:05.720 --> 01:10:11.192
It is, if what you care about is predictions of measurement outcomes,

01:10:11.192 --> 01:10:11.864
the numbers...

01:10:11.864 --> 01:10:17.093
The numbers, they could be committed both ways, but the explanatory power is not the same.

01:10:17.093 --> 01:10:20.467
So, power, yes, but also structure. There's another way we could...

01:10:20.467 --> 01:10:26.973
So for a realist, we're in the business of saying, well, physics is not just about calculating predictions.

01:10:26.973 --> 01:10:32.424
It's of course nice to calculate predictions, but physics is in the business of trying

01:10:32.424 --> 01:10:36.456
to figure out how the world works. And we're aware that all our work is guesswork,

01:10:36.456 --> 01:10:40.040
it's conjectural, but we're going to stress test our ideas, we're going to back them

01:10:40.040 --> 01:10:44.942
against the wall. However, if you come up with a theory and we say "the state of the

01:10:44.942 --> 01:10:48.694
system is," what we mean is that the state of the system is.

01:10:48.694 --> 01:10:53.808
It's a conjecture about how the system is out there, independent of our preferences and

01:10:53.808 --> 01:10:54.373
our opinions.

01:10:54.373 --> 01:10:59.213
So if you're a realist, then you say, hold on, that gives us two different stories.

01:10:59.213 --> 01:11:05.385
The Schrödinger story is that we have a ket, a state vector or a wave function,

01:11:05.385 --> 01:11:08.740
it's called by different names, that is evolving in time.

01:11:08.740 --> 01:11:14.507
And the Heisenberg story is that we have a bunch of matrices evolving in time.

01:11:14.507 --> 01:11:19.300
Now, we could declare these two theories equivalent even for a realist,

01:11:19.300 --> 01:11:25.395
if we would have what the mathematicians would call an isomorphism between the two structures.

01:11:25.395 --> 01:11:29.864
The interesting part is when you start declaring isomorphism between structures that

01:11:29.864 --> 01:11:33.416
prima facie do not look like they're the same.

01:11:33.416 --> 01:11:42.787
Suppose I have the natural numbers, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, and I have two copies of them,

01:11:42.787 --> 01:11:49.103
plus I add a zero. Plus I tell you that one copy is kind of the negative sign of the

01:11:49.103 --> 01:11:53.122
other copy. But it's really like two sets of natural numbers going this way,

01:11:53.122 --> 01:11:57.080
and one of them has some negative signs, so that the arithmetic has changed,

01:11:57.080 --> 01:11:59.080
and I prescribe you the arithmetic in the precise way.

01:11:59.080 --> 01:12:02.620
I don't want to go into the details, because we're going to be wasting time.

01:12:02.620 --> 01:12:06.576
But then someone could realize, hey, hold on, we could have the integers,

01:12:06.576 --> 01:12:10.255
which goes all the way plus infinity to minus infinity.

01:12:10.255 --> 01:12:13.570
So one, two, three, four, five, and then we have zero, minus one,

01:12:13.570 --> 01:12:17.906
minus two, minus... And one could prove that, oh, well, the two structures are isomorphic.

01:12:17.906 --> 01:12:21.935
Because I came up with two sort of stories of telling you, but one of them,

01:12:21.935 --> 01:12:27.100
I was kind of hiding the fact that I had negative numbers, the other one I was making explicit.

01:12:27.100 --> 01:12:32.409
But who cares, because we have a one-to-one map: for every number in theory one,

01:12:32.409 --> 01:12:35.664
there's a corresponding number in theory two, and vice versa.

01:12:35.664 --> 01:12:40.341
And plus, that's just a bijection so far, but the isomorphism also preserves the structures.

01:12:40.341 --> 01:12:45.580
So if I have addition in one theory, and also have a counterpart of the addition in the

01:12:45.580 --> 01:12:49.809
second theory. That's why you go like, "Oh, it's the same thing." And a realist would

01:12:49.809 --> 01:12:53.315
have been convinced that the Heisenberg picture and the Schrödinger picture are equivalent,

01:12:53.315 --> 01:12:58.655
also for a realist, if you would have such a one-to-one map,

01:12:58.655 --> 01:13:02.323
bijective map and isomorphic, that also preserves the structures,

01:13:02.323 --> 01:13:05.567
like time evolution and what happens when we...

01:13:05.567 --> 01:13:08.877
and so on. But there's no such map.

01:13:08.877 --> 01:13:15.960
So the general account is that if you give me the Heisenberg picture description of the

01:13:15.960 --> 01:13:21.651
system, it corresponds to a unique Schrödinger picture description of the system,

01:13:21.651 --> 01:13:26.720
so there's a unique wave function, ket. But not the other way around.

01:13:26.720 --> 01:13:31.260
If you only specify the wave function of the system, the state vector of the system,

01:13:31.260 --> 01:13:35.676
the Schrödinger picture description of the system, there are many possible Heisenberg

01:13:35.676 --> 01:13:38.700
picture states that correspond to it.

01:13:38.700 --> 01:13:46.036
Basically, there's more information captured in the Heisenberg system than the Schrödinger

01:13:46.036 --> 01:13:50.084
system, which means that one is basically richer, the other lesser.

01:13:50.084 --> 01:13:53.498
So you can only do things one way, not the other way, basically.

01:13:53.498 --> 01:13:56.284
So I'm aware that some experts listening here might say, "Well,

01:13:56.284 --> 01:14:00.590
the true account of the Schrödinger picture is not just the time-evolved state.

01:14:00.590 --> 01:14:04.880
It's also the dynamical operators," these U's I've put in the middle,

01:14:04.880 --> 01:14:08.460
"alongside the initial algebra of observables," these matrices in the middle.

01:14:08.460 --> 01:14:15.476
But then, sure, of course, because you're giving all the ingredients of quantum theory.

01:14:15.476 --> 01:14:22.698
But no one declares that the state in the Schrödinger picture is this thing that is enriched

01:14:22.698 --> 01:14:27.341
with a part of the evolution operators, but not all of it, because you still want locality.

01:14:27.341 --> 01:14:32.626
So you don't want that your description of Alice's system depends on whatever Bob is doing.

01:14:32.626 --> 01:14:38.466
I said no one, modulo the fact that the work of Mordecai Waegell at Chapman University

01:14:38.466 --> 01:14:41.443
is kind of taking seriously these locality structures.

01:14:41.443 --> 01:14:46.664
You can have them, and he's developing Schrödinger picture versions of what it would

01:14:46.664 --> 01:14:51.380
be like. But he would also agree that the objects he's calling states are nothing like

01:14:51.380 --> 01:14:54.964
the usual Schrödinger state. So we have this many-to-one ontology,

01:14:54.964 --> 01:14:57.159
so why would we work with more structures?

01:14:57.159 --> 01:15:01.441
Yeah, of course, if we're still in the shut up and calculate framework,

01:15:01.441 --> 01:15:04.220
it doesn't make a difference, the better.

01:15:04.220 --> 01:15:09.113
I want to crank up numbers. But if we're in the business of trying to explain the world,

01:15:09.113 --> 01:15:11.540
we want to take what works best.

01:15:11.540 --> 01:15:19.087
Yes. And it turns out that the Heisenberg picture descriptions provide a fully local

01:15:19.087 --> 01:15:26.044
account of local systems. At least to me, was news when I read the work of David Deutsch

01:15:26.044 --> 01:15:31.316
and Patrick Hayden, published in 2000, worked out in 1999, where they spell out what

01:15:31.316 --> 01:15:35.780
Heisenberg picture quantum theory looks like for quantum computation.

01:15:35.780 --> 01:15:39.544
And in short, it provides what looks like the impossible.

01:15:39.544 --> 01:15:42.152
It provides a way to describe entangled systems.

01:15:42.152 --> 01:15:45.120
So an entangled pair of qubits: you have a qubit, I have a qubit,

01:15:45.120 --> 01:15:48.511
my qubit has its own descriptor. They had to call it by another name,

01:15:48.511 --> 01:15:53.409
but really it's a state. But if you use the word state, people load it and associate

01:15:53.409 --> 01:15:57.346
it with Schrödinger, so they call it a descriptor.

01:15:57.346 --> 01:16:01.791
And my descriptor remains unchanged if you play with your system,

01:16:01.791 --> 01:16:03.897
which is this locality aspect.

01:16:03.897 --> 01:16:04.397
Yes.

01:16:04.397 --> 01:16:08.071
Schrödinger picture descriptions can sometimes use the so-called reduced density matrices,

01:16:08.071 --> 01:16:11.860
and they have this property: the reduced density matrix of a system is unchanged when

01:16:11.860 --> 01:16:17.038
somebody else plays with his system. But the reduced density matrices are too thin a description.

01:16:17.038 --> 01:16:23.393
If we put both of our reduced density matrices together, it's a way of describing systems

01:16:23.393 --> 01:16:26.946
in the Schrödinger picture, but that omits too much important information,

01:16:26.946 --> 01:16:31.828
because the collection of two reduced density matrices cannot get back the whole system

01:16:31.828 --> 01:16:34.551
when they're entangled. Whereas descriptors have that property.

01:16:34.551 --> 01:16:37.376
So not only are they local, like the reduced density matrices,

01:16:37.376 --> 01:16:41.907
but if you put them back together, you can recover the whole Schrödinger entangled state.

01:16:41.907 --> 01:16:46.244
Or, if you're an advocate of the Heisenberg picture, you don't care so much about recovering

01:16:46.244 --> 01:16:49.876
the Schrödinger state, but it permits to cash out the distributions of any measurements

01:16:49.876 --> 01:16:52.218
that might be performed on the joint system.

01:16:52.218 --> 01:16:58.796
We have to carry out the calculations of what happens to these crystals when Alice measures

01:16:58.796 --> 01:17:03.244
and when Bob measures. There's a lot to recover there, because when Alice will measure

01:17:03.244 --> 01:17:13.496
her system, she will be affected by the system in a way that Alice's descriptor will

01:17:13.496 --> 01:17:22.825
evolve into a sum of two entities. This was developed by Sam Kuipers and David Deutsch

01:17:22.825 --> 01:17:29.386
in 2021. They basically recovered the basics of Everett's analysis in the Heisenberg

01:17:29.386 --> 01:17:33.965
picture for descriptors. So whenever with Everett we realized that we had a sum of two

01:17:33.965 --> 01:17:37.106
state vectors, and that these two state vectors no longer interact with each other,

01:17:37.106 --> 01:17:40.366
they become autonomous, and they have a Charles who sees green light and a Charles who

01:17:40.366 --> 01:17:44.860
sees red light, well, what's the story with descriptors, with Heisenberg picture descriptors?

01:17:44.860 --> 01:17:53.000
And here it is, roughly speaking: you have an Alice evolving into Alice sees zero,

01:17:53.000 --> 01:17:58.465
plus, literally a plus... therefore there's something else to capture.

01:17:58.465 --> 01:18:01.386
Everett's idea, where we don't need to declare that only one exists.

01:18:01.386 --> 01:18:05.335
We make peace with the fact that ascribing to is pretending that there's something bigger,

01:18:05.335 --> 01:18:08.113
and we're only a substructure of that something bigger.

01:18:08.113 --> 01:18:11.487
So I'm Alice who sees zero, there's Alice who sees one.

01:18:11.487 --> 01:18:16.700
If we were to compute probabilities at that moment, we would compute that Alice obtains

01:18:16.700 --> 01:18:20.407
zero with probability a half, Alice obtains one with probability a half.

01:18:20.407 --> 01:18:23.895
But really, we don't care so much about priorities at that stage.

01:18:23.895 --> 01:18:26.606
We carry on. We have two outgoing Alices.

01:18:26.606 --> 01:18:29.776
They don't see each other, and it's fully local.

01:18:29.776 --> 01:18:36.201
So we don't have this awkward thing where the state was described by something that also

01:18:36.201 --> 01:18:40.673
depended on Bob. Now we have only Alice's local descriptor spreading into two entities,

01:18:40.673 --> 01:18:41.420
autonomous entities.

01:18:41.420 --> 01:18:46.332
Right. So instead of having the faster than light communication or something,

01:18:46.332 --> 01:18:52.380
Alice just gets entangled with the descriptor, and that's how the puzzle is answered.

01:18:52.380 --> 01:18:58.300
Well, not yet. We haven't got to the 85, but we're getting there.

01:18:58.300 --> 01:19:05.717
It was a long detour. We were discussing the CHSH game maybe 30 minutes ago,

01:19:05.717 --> 01:19:10.204
but it was a long detour to explain the measurement problem correctly,

01:19:10.204 --> 01:19:12.997
the value of jumping into the Heisenberg picture description,

01:19:12.997 --> 01:19:15.056
and now we're finally going to cash it out.

01:19:15.056 --> 01:19:20.115
The first thing to mention is that splitting of Alice is purely local.

01:19:20.115 --> 01:19:26.004
Alice splits into two entities because her local descriptor splits into two entities.

01:19:26.004 --> 01:19:32.273
And when Bob measures his crystal, he will likewise locally split into two Bobs,

01:19:32.273 --> 01:19:37.460
Bob who sees zero, Bob who sees one. And those branches are not tied,

01:19:37.460 --> 01:19:39.060
they're not identified yet.

01:19:39.060 --> 01:19:45.460
What happens there is, this is my Alices, this is my Bobs.

01:19:45.460 --> 01:19:50.277
Alice saw zero, Bob saw zero, in the Schrödinger picture, already tied.

01:19:50.277 --> 01:19:54.479
Yes. And so we kind of know that when they're going to compare their results,

01:19:54.479 --> 01:19:57.260
Alice who sees zero is going to meet with a Bob who sees zero,

01:19:57.260 --> 01:20:00.260
and Alice who sees one is going to meet with a Bob who sees one.

01:20:00.260 --> 01:20:04.485
But in the Heisenberg picture so far, it's just local entities.

01:20:04.485 --> 01:20:10.820
Of course, because we still have a deterministic theory, we can compute what would happen

01:20:10.820 --> 01:20:16.378
if they then compare their notes. And we would find that Alice who sees zero meets with

01:20:16.378 --> 01:20:20.593
a Bob who sees zero with 85% divided by two probability, Alice who sees one will meet

01:20:20.593 --> 01:20:23.849
with the Bob who sees one with 85% divided by two probability,

01:20:23.849 --> 01:20:26.660
and the mismatches with 15% probability.

01:20:26.660 --> 01:20:35.000
But that's kind of going too fast. What matters is, and that's an idea as old as Don

01:20:35.000 --> 01:20:41.140
Page and Frank Tipler, is the idea that there's an interesting mechanism coming up here.

01:20:41.140 --> 01:20:44.698
Sorry, I just said that Don Page and Frank Tipler are old.

01:20:44.698 --> 01:20:55.460
As old as their work. So Don Page was studying the comparison interaction in the EPR setting.

01:20:55.460 --> 01:20:59.040
Tipler raised it up for the Bell scenario, but he was studying in the Schrödinger picture,

01:20:59.040 --> 01:21:03.900
so could not cash out as sharp an idea as what we're coming up here.

01:21:03.900 --> 01:21:09.836
And also, Deutsch and Hayden studied the Bell scenario, and they were after localizing

01:21:09.836 --> 01:21:14.004
the information flow, but they correctly identified, I believe that would be section

01:21:14.004 --> 01:21:21.911
four of their paper, that a Bell inequality violation is only done once Alice and Bob

01:21:21.911 --> 01:21:25.190
come back together. And so that's crucial.

01:21:25.190 --> 01:21:28.948
And you might say, well, what is the change?

01:21:28.948 --> 01:21:32.879
Well, it changes the fact that now, since we have multiple Alices,

01:21:32.879 --> 01:21:38.249
one who sees zero, one who sees one, multiple Bobs, one who sees zero and one who sees

01:21:38.249 --> 01:21:43.093
none, it's no longer clear how this is going to generate four joint records,

01:21:43.093 --> 01:21:50.088
the 00 record, 01, 10 and 11 record. In a single world orthodoxy,

01:21:50.088 --> 01:21:54.316
if there's only a single world, I have Alice who sees zero here and Bob who sees one

01:21:54.316 --> 01:21:55.284
here, there's only one answer.

01:21:55.284 --> 01:21:55.784
Yes.

01:21:55.784 --> 01:21:59.874
When they're going to join their results, it's going to be zero and one.

01:21:59.874 --> 01:22:04.320
Nothing can happen. But since we're in a quantum orthodoxy...

01:22:04.320 --> 01:22:06.949
Yeah. We have multiple Alices, multiple Bobs.

01:22:06.949 --> 01:22:09.920
Then you might say, "Oh, there's freedom here."

01:22:09.920 --> 01:22:18.160
Yes. Even though it's 50, Alice 0, Alice 1, 50-50, if the computer property is there,

01:22:18.160 --> 01:22:19.496
and same with Bob.

01:22:19.496 --> 01:22:25.058
The thing is, when we look at the descriptors, they're made of algebraic structures that

01:22:25.058 --> 01:22:31.760
may interplay, and that's precisely what is ending up happening.

01:22:31.760 --> 01:22:37.970
So what I calculated in my Explaining Bell Locally paper, which is basically the technical

01:22:37.970 --> 01:22:44.260
version of this book chapter, is that we need to calculate what happens to a joint record.

01:22:44.260 --> 01:22:47.660
A Charlie in the middle is a four-level system.

01:22:47.660 --> 01:22:53.422
He's back on Earth, and he's waiting to write down the communication of Alice and waiting

01:22:53.422 --> 01:22:58.151
to write down the communication of Bob into one single localized record that will be

01:22:58.151 --> 01:22:59.320
the joint record.

01:22:59.320 --> 01:23:03.400
And what are we going to apply as a theory for that Charlie?

01:23:03.400 --> 01:23:07.540
Are we going to apply A, our pet theory of what classical theory should be like,

01:23:07.540 --> 01:23:10.640
or what classical information processing should be like?

01:23:10.640 --> 01:23:12.400
Or are we going to apply B, quantum theory?

01:23:12.400 --> 01:23:17.700
Because the name of the game is to explain the classical with quantum theory.

01:23:17.700 --> 01:23:20.620
Obviously B. But this is where intuitions can go wrong.

01:23:20.620 --> 01:23:22.080
Because we might say, "Oh no, that changes nothing.

01:23:22.080 --> 01:23:26.963
Let's just do a shortcut and say that Charlie's record is going to be an element in the

01:23:26.963 --> 01:23:35.638
set 00, 01, 10, 11." Well, sorry, but sets 00 comma 01 comma 10 comma 11 are discrete

01:23:35.638 --> 01:23:38.029
structures, which are very alien to quantum theory.

01:23:38.029 --> 01:23:38.529
Yes.

01:23:38.529 --> 01:23:42.450
What you want to do is to apply quantum mechanics to Charlie.

01:23:42.450 --> 01:23:47.208
And so what happens is, when he processes Alice's outcome...

01:23:47.208 --> 01:23:47.708
Yes.

01:23:47.708 --> 01:23:50.687
He also locally splits into two instances.

01:23:50.687 --> 01:23:51.187
Yes.

01:23:51.187 --> 01:23:56.338
Charlie who sees Alice with zero and Charlie who sees Alice with one.

01:23:56.338 --> 01:23:56.838
Right.

01:23:56.838 --> 01:23:58.609
These measures are still 50-50.

01:23:58.609 --> 01:23:59.109
Yes.

01:23:59.109 --> 01:24:05.482
But then, when he processes Bob, each of these sub-measures splits again,

01:24:05.482 --> 01:24:12.137
and the split is non-trivial. Charlie who saw Alice zero now splits 35,

01:24:12.137 --> 01:24:24.248
no, 42.5, 8.5. Charlie is going to see Alice who saw zero and Bob who saw zero.

01:24:24.248 --> 01:24:25.040
Yes.

01:24:25.040 --> 01:24:31.124
And the 8.5 is going to be Charlie saw Alice who saw zero and Bob saw one,

01:24:31.124 --> 01:24:34.960
the mismatch. And similarly for the other Charlie.

01:24:34.960 --> 01:24:40.987
And so we have four emerging Charlies with exactly the right weights of the CHSH distribution.

01:24:40.987 --> 01:24:50.356
Really, the whole point of this exercise is to then show that you can have this 85% while

01:24:50.356 --> 01:24:56.200
not having faster than light communication, while not requiring retrocausal models,

01:24:56.200 --> 01:25:01.938
and while having a fully local explanation, which is very, very powerful.

01:25:01.938 --> 01:25:05.493
And I would like to add, without wishful thinking either.

01:25:05.493 --> 01:25:12.192
It's not just "it would be nice if we could have that." We also have that by studying

01:25:12.192 --> 01:25:15.310
unitary quantum theory in the Heisenberg picture.

01:25:15.310 --> 01:25:18.485
So I think it's important, because unlike the superdeterministic program,

01:25:18.485 --> 01:25:19.784
say, who's trying to...

01:25:19.784 --> 01:25:22.056
Yeah, we're not making crazy things about...

01:25:22.056 --> 01:25:24.278
And be willing to reconsider huge hypotheses.

01:25:24.278 --> 01:25:28.762
Yes, I'm sympathetic to that, but bold conjectures are kind of hard to come by,

01:25:28.762 --> 01:25:36.480
to be good. And here it looks like I'm positing this radical story where Alice splits,

01:25:36.480 --> 01:25:39.369
and somehow the way she meets with Bob is unintuitive.

01:25:39.369 --> 01:25:43.380
And, "How did you come up with this?" Well, calculate it.

01:25:43.380 --> 01:25:46.355
Yeah, it's literally the math.

01:25:46.355 --> 01:25:51.191
Exactly. If you calculate it in the Heisenberg picture of unitary quantum theory.

01:25:51.191 --> 01:25:54.296
So I think that's also the important thing to mention.

01:25:54.296 --> 01:25:57.312
Yeah, it's not just wanting to save the program with a local story.

01:25:57.312 --> 01:25:59.790
It's a local story that follows from quantum mechanics.

01:25:59.790 --> 01:26:01.960
Yeah, it's all rooted in the mathematics.

01:26:01.960 --> 01:26:05.143
There's two remarks I'd like to make, if I could.

01:26:05.143 --> 01:26:05.790
Let's go.

01:26:05.790 --> 01:26:13.528
One of them is about relativity. I said that Alice who sees zero is not yet identified

01:26:13.528 --> 01:26:19.408
with Bob who sees zero. Could I be more precise?

01:26:19.408 --> 01:26:19.996
Yes.

01:26:19.996 --> 01:26:26.738
It seems like it's unavoidable that the Alice who sees zero is going to meet with the

01:26:26.738 --> 01:26:31.836
Bob after Alice has measured and after Bob has measured.

01:26:31.836 --> 01:26:38.270
We call this a hyper sheet of space. It's a sheet of space in space-time,

01:26:38.270 --> 01:26:40.620
okay? Hypersurface, it's usually called.

01:26:40.620 --> 01:26:45.040
Time goes this way. But now I'm after both measurement interactions.

01:26:45.040 --> 01:26:50.787
It seems like an absolute that Alice who sees zero is going to meet up,

01:26:50.787 --> 01:26:55.874
with sub-measure 85%, with Bob who sees zero.

01:26:55.874 --> 01:27:03.804
But it's not an absolute. It's not an absolute, because the Bob who sees zero and the

01:27:03.804 --> 01:27:09.162
Bob who sees one, we said it's hard, but in principle they can unmeasure.

01:27:09.162 --> 01:27:14.740
If they're able to run after all the witnesses of the measurement interaction,

01:27:14.740 --> 01:27:22.709
they can untangle, reproduce the crystal's state, change the way they turn their crystal

01:27:22.709 --> 01:27:29.301
before measuring, and re-measure. And that would basically screw Alice's bet.

01:27:29.301 --> 01:27:29.851
Yes.

01:27:29.851 --> 01:27:32.433
Because then she would meet with a different Bob.

01:27:32.433 --> 01:27:38.088
For example, we could arrange the twisting of the crystals such that it's sure that she

01:27:38.088 --> 01:27:43.568
meets with Bob 1. So Alice 0 meets with Bob 1 if this unmeasurement is performed,

01:27:43.568 --> 01:27:44.240
and re-twisting.

01:27:44.240 --> 01:27:50.789
And I think an analogy I like is that it's exactly similar to the traveling twins.

01:27:50.789 --> 01:27:54.120
A listener might say, "Oh, the traveling twins are already counterintuitive,

01:27:54.120 --> 01:28:00.768
but I'm going to put another layer of counterintuitiveness." The typical scenario is

01:28:00.768 --> 01:28:04.656
that we have Charlie and Dalton, I'm changing names.

01:28:04.656 --> 01:28:10.604
They're twins. Charlie stays on Earth. Dalton goes on a big voyage in the galaxy.

01:28:10.604 --> 01:28:15.500
And while he's far away, one could ask, suppose they eventually reunite,

01:28:15.500 --> 01:28:20.432
who will be the younger? And you might remember from your relativity courses,

01:28:20.432 --> 01:28:25.046
or some of the good YouTube videos you might have watched, that the traveler is going

01:28:25.046 --> 01:28:28.240
to be the younger, and that's super counterintuitive.

01:28:28.240 --> 01:28:35.280
That's true if we assume the continuation of the story, which is that Dalton comes back

01:28:35.280 --> 01:28:39.501
to Earth and Charlie doesn't move. But that was not my question.

01:28:39.501 --> 01:28:44.080
My question was, Charlie stayed on Earth, Dalton went on a voyage,

01:28:44.080 --> 01:28:47.280
and while he was far away, I asked the question.

01:28:47.280 --> 01:28:47.780
Yeah.

01:28:47.780 --> 01:28:52.293
But suppose that I make a twist. A different continuation of the story is such that Charlie,

01:28:52.293 --> 01:28:58.189
because he's waited so long on Earth, now has access to way more powerful means of transportation.

01:28:58.189 --> 01:28:58.689
Yeah.

01:28:58.689 --> 01:29:02.476
And he goes to a different galaxy and comes back, by the time...

01:29:02.476 --> 01:29:07.316
compute your speed of light limits. But suppose he's able to reach far closer the frontier

01:29:07.316 --> 01:29:11.380
of the speed of light, compared to the means of transportation given to Dalton.

01:29:11.380 --> 01:29:15.920
When they reunite, Charlie will be the younger, because he will be considered the traveler

01:29:15.920 --> 01:29:19.856
with respect to Dalton, which almost looks stationary in his poor little trip around

01:29:19.856 --> 01:29:23.312
the galaxy. So the continuation of the story matters.

01:29:23.312 --> 01:29:27.468
And this is precisely why we cannot declare whose twin is going to be the younger when

01:29:27.468 --> 01:29:31.565
they reunite, until we have an actual implementation of this reunion.

01:29:31.565 --> 01:29:39.111
Same thing here. Alice zero meets with Bob zero if we continue the story as it is expected.

01:29:39.111 --> 01:29:44.040
But if Bob unmeasures, twists the crystal and re-measures, the continuation may change.

01:29:44.040 --> 01:29:48.140
I think you mentioned a second thing you wanted to mention.

01:29:48.140 --> 01:29:54.320
I think it's important, because at that stage, I hope every competent physicist would

01:29:54.320 --> 01:29:59.600
be extremely critical of the account I've given, saying, "Charles,

01:29:59.600 --> 01:30:06.219
that's kind of nice, but there's one thing we know." Where this uneven skewing of the

01:30:06.219 --> 01:30:12.588
measures, when Alice meets, or Charlie, when he processes Bob's signal,

01:30:12.588 --> 01:30:16.852
starts splitting like 42.5 and 8.5, that looks like a quantum effect.

01:30:16.852 --> 01:30:21.464
And maybe most people will be willing to think that after measurement,

01:30:21.464 --> 01:30:26.038
we can keep a quantum ontology like Everett did, by having many worlds,

01:30:26.038 --> 01:30:30.988
and, okay, fine. But typically, once we reach measurement, and many,

01:30:30.988 --> 01:30:34.836
many records, no more quantum effects happen.

01:30:34.836 --> 01:30:35.336
Yes.

01:30:35.336 --> 01:30:43.686
So how dare I pretend that this uneven skewing of the media part of the work?

01:30:43.686 --> 01:30:54.000
Great question. Good criticism. In my Explaining Bell Locally paper,

01:30:54.000 --> 01:31:01.360
the second last section is titled Classicality, because I have this precise case to answer.

01:31:01.360 --> 01:31:09.096
And the answer is, when you're playing the CHSH game, do not mess with the crystals while

01:31:09.096 --> 01:31:12.061
they are on their way to Mercury and Jupiter.

01:31:12.061 --> 01:31:15.163
They're extremely precious. They need to remain shielded and quantum,

01:31:15.163 --> 01:31:16.155
otherwise you're ruining...

01:31:16.155 --> 01:31:16.655
Yes.

01:31:16.655 --> 01:31:20.240
That is well known. This is what people will, in the common language,

01:31:20.240 --> 01:31:23.929
say: "Oh, it's a quantum system, it needs to remain quantum." Sure.

01:31:23.929 --> 01:31:26.762
But after Alice's measurement, we don't care.

01:31:26.762 --> 01:31:28.786
There's so many witnesses.

01:31:28.786 --> 01:31:30.560
Yeah.

01:31:30.560 --> 01:31:37.930
And so I modeled many witnesses after Alice's measurement, in the way that there could

01:31:37.930 --> 01:31:42.945
be an environmental system that also interacts and keeps measuring Alice,

01:31:42.945 --> 01:31:48.060
so that Alice is effectively evolving into a decohered state,

01:31:48.060 --> 01:31:52.668
with many witnesses. And you model this with quantum theory.

01:31:52.668 --> 01:31:56.053
Of course, if you would compute the reduced density matrices,

01:31:56.053 --> 01:31:59.867
you would get this usual story we've been discussing.

01:31:59.867 --> 01:32:04.143
But you model this not as "this magic happens, a system becomes decohered,

01:32:04.143 --> 01:32:07.416
and therefore classical." No, no, no. We're after explaining classicality,

01:32:07.416 --> 01:32:14.320
not positing it. Well, what I said is in a way true, but don't take classicality as being fundamental.

01:32:14.320 --> 01:32:22.330
So the descriptor of Alice inherits many structures that is kind of a sign of having

01:32:22.330 --> 01:32:26.427
interacted with many degrees of freedom of their environment.

01:32:26.427 --> 01:32:32.560
So I'm modeling this classicality, and yet this skewed branching,

01:32:32.560 --> 01:32:38.524
rebranching of Charlie, still works. So it answers the case.

01:32:38.524 --> 01:32:45.269
I think the big lesson here is, I've insisted on that already,

01:32:45.269 --> 01:32:46.955
but it's quantum theory.

01:32:46.955 --> 01:32:47.455
Yes.

01:32:47.455 --> 01:32:50.469
Not necessarily the quantum theory we're all used to work with.

01:32:50.469 --> 01:32:53.991
It's the Heisenberg picture. We're not chained.

01:32:53.991 --> 01:32:59.920
And every time there's something like comparing notes, you have to think,

01:32:59.920 --> 01:33:01.688
"Oh, how is that done physically?"

01:33:01.688 --> 01:33:04.931
Yes, it's part of quantum theory. Of course.

01:33:04.931 --> 01:33:08.817
Whenever we write notes, it doesn't come out from thin air.

01:33:08.817 --> 01:33:09.916
Yes.

01:33:09.916 --> 01:33:15.004
We're actually taking a pen and writing it down, and that's a physical process.

01:33:15.004 --> 01:33:18.720
And also, a little reaction to your account, which is amazing.

01:33:18.720 --> 01:33:23.591
Wherever you use the word entanglement, you could have used also local splitting of Alice

01:33:23.591 --> 01:33:27.026
into two entities, and then same for Bob.

01:33:27.026 --> 01:33:30.674
And then Charlie locally splits when he processes Alice's input first,

01:33:30.674 --> 01:33:36.551
she splits into two, and then each of those sub-versions splits again into two as he's

01:33:36.551 --> 01:33:40.905
acquiring the signal by Bob. Because sometimes entanglement,

01:33:40.905 --> 01:33:45.580
especially for a non-expert, may sound like a link.

01:33:45.580 --> 01:33:48.960
Yeah. Entanglement still exists in the Heisenberg picture, of course,

01:33:48.960 --> 01:33:54.320
but it does not have the definition of having one single state for two objects,

01:33:54.320 --> 01:34:01.397
because Heisenberg picture quantum theory is able to literally have fully local and complete

01:34:01.397 --> 01:34:05.705
description of individual systems. So entanglement typically means,

01:34:05.705 --> 01:34:14.270
in the Heisenberg picture, that if systems A and B are entangled and you only have access

01:34:14.270 --> 01:34:20.720
to system A, you won't be able to produce a sharp outcome with deterministic,

01:34:20.720 --> 01:34:23.940
"I will only see zero," outgoing branch.

01:34:23.940 --> 01:34:24.860
Right.

01:34:24.860 --> 01:34:31.064
And same for the other one. But if I put them back together and I make them play with

01:34:31.064 --> 01:34:35.138
them, then I could produce a sharp outcome for the joint systems.

01:34:35.138 --> 01:34:38.620
Well, thank you very much, Charles. This was a pleasure.

01:34:38.620 --> 01:34:42.940
We'll have to do a second episode to tackle everything else that we have planned for today.

01:34:42.940 --> 01:34:45.226
But thank you so much for your time. This was great.

01:34:45.226 --> 01:34:48.332
It was a true pleasure. Thank you, Maxime, for this fascinating conversation.

01:34:48.332 --> 01:34:54.647
And if you want more, have a look at Bold Conjectures, Volume 2,

01:34:54.647 --> 01:34:58.380
edited by Logan Chipkin. It's a fun collection of essays.

01:34:58.380 --> 01:35:04.005
I had the great honor to write pieces with Sam Kuipers, Chiara Marletto,

01:35:04.005 --> 01:35:07.334
Vlatko Vedral, David Wallace, Julian Barbour, and many more,

01:35:07.334 --> 01:35:11.420
Maria Violaris, Simone Rijavec. Many nice, interesting thinkers in this volume,

01:35:11.420 --> 01:35:14.437
and it's written for an accessible readership.

01:35:14.437 --> 01:35:19.500
You're truly at the edge of physics if you read this book.

01:35:19.500 --> 01:35:23.563
Literally, without mathematics. We want to distill the ideas.

01:35:23.563 --> 01:35:25.458
Yeah, exactly. And this is your copy.

01:35:25.458 --> 01:35:26.584
Thank you so much.

01:35:26.584 --> 01:35:30.576
Awesome. Well, see you back soon.
